course: dictionary
lesson: 4772
title: Howl and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and howl has several. Read the words around it to find the right one. «Coyotes howl, yip and bark to keep in touch with family» tells you that howl is a sound an animal makes: a long, loud cry.
explain: A person can howl too, when they cry loudly in pain, anger or sadness. The wind can howl in a storm. Ask yourself who or what is howling, and the subject tells you the meaning. To check, swap in another word, such as "wail", and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: In «it went in off Liam's knee, and everyone howled», the clue is that everyone is making a big noise together, so howled means laughed very loudly. Howl can also be a noun: a long, loud cry, as in «a howl of pain».
fact: Howl means a long, loud cry.
fact: «Dingoes» are wild dogs that howl rather than bark, and a howl is often a sound that carries a long way.
fact: «Howl with laughter» means to laugh very loudly.
fact: «Howl at the moon» and «howling wind» help create a spooky or wild mood in a story.
fact: Words with several meanings are called multiple-meaning words: check the context to choose the right one.
exercise: «Coyotes howl, yip and bark to keep in touch with family.» Why do coyotes howl? | To sleep at night | *To keep in touch with family | To catch fish | To hide from the rain
exercise: «It went in off Liam's knee, and everyone howled.» What does howled mean here? | Went to sleep | Cried very quietly | *Laughed very loudly | Ran away fast
exercise: In «the wind gave a howl», what is a howl? | A quiet sigh | *A long, loud cry | A kind of tree | A cake
test: «The wind began to howl across the moor.» What is the wind doing? | Making a cake | Sleeping peacefully | *Blowing hard with a loud, wailing sound | Melting the snow
test: Sam says howl means to bark softly. What is wrong with his idea? | Howl means a soft bark, so he is right | *Howl means a long, loud cry, not a soft bark | Howl means to whisper
exam: In «Dingoes are wild dogs... they howl rather than bark», what is the difference between a howl and a bark? | They mean exactly the same thing | *A howl is a long, loud cry, and a bark is a different sound | A howl is a short, sharp sound, and a bark is a long, loud cry | A bark is only made by cats
